WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.090
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:23.360 --> 00:30.320
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

3
00:30.320 --> 00:35.840
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

4
00:35.840 --> 00:38.440
♪ I don't understand ♪

5
00:38.440 --> 00:43.920
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

6
00:43.920 --> 00:48.720
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪

7
00:49.120 --> 00:55.080
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

8
00:57.080 --> 00:59.600
Do you like being a whore that much? Is that why you lied to me?

9
00:59.960 --> 01:02.040
Was your life so hard when you're with me?

10
01:02.040 --> 01:03.400
Why did you have to accept the job again?

11
01:03.400 --> 01:06.040
- Sis Mol needs money to... - I asked if you didn't have enough money.

12
01:06.040 --> 01:08.680
Was your life so hard that you had to accept the job again?

13
01:08.680 --> 01:10.560
I'll set a date for you to meet my family.

14
01:10.560 --> 01:12.080
Speaking as someone in the same field.

15
01:12.080 --> 01:14.240
There are certain types of women you shouldn't bring into your home.

16
01:14.240 --> 01:15.560
Are you and him...

17
01:16.120 --> 01:17.000
We're together.

18
01:17.000 --> 01:19.200
You went official with Techin too.

19
01:19.200 --> 01:20.400
I missed you so much.

20
01:24.240 --> 01:25.920
You two haven't talked?

21
01:30.080 --> 01:31.080
We have.

22
01:31.720 --> 01:32.840
Several times.

23
01:33.479 --> 01:35.240
Is she coming around?

24
01:38.039 --> 01:39.360
I ran into her today

25
01:39.920 --> 01:41.800
while I was out for a meal with Mr. Techin.

26
01:42.840 --> 01:45.640
Wow, good timing.

27
01:46.600 --> 01:47.720
Yeah.

28
01:47.720 --> 01:49.479
And did you explain it to her?

29
01:50.320 --> 01:51.759
She's dating someone new.

30
01:52.560 --> 01:53.479
No way.

31
01:55.160 --> 01:58.160
What someone new? She loves you so much.

32
02:00.120 --> 02:01.200
It's my fault

33
02:02.800 --> 02:04.840
for not telling the truth from the beginning.

34
02:07.000 --> 02:08.840
It's too late to fix anything now.

35
02:18.520 --> 02:20.000
Please come in.

36
02:23.800 --> 02:25.440
Please come in.

37
02:25.440 --> 02:27.000
Please, please come in.

38
02:27.760 --> 02:29.240
Please have a seat.

39
02:31.760 --> 02:34.280
Please have a seat and relax.

40
02:35.640 --> 02:37.400
I saw you looking at the girl back there.

41
02:40.440 --> 02:41.920
Ugh! Pat!

42
02:41.920 --> 02:43.160
- Pat! - What?

43
02:44.160 --> 02:45.440
Hurry!

44
02:45.440 --> 02:46.520
What?

45
02:46.520 --> 02:47.880
What's going on?

46
02:47.880 --> 02:49.240
- Ms. Peem is here. - Huh?

47
02:49.240 --> 02:50.320
And she brought her friends.

48
02:50.320 --> 02:51.240
Why is she here?

49
02:51.240 --> 02:53.360
I don't know. Just go greet her.

50
02:53.360 --> 02:56.360
Alright, you go tell Parn that Ms. Peem is here, before she goes on stage.

51
02:56.360 --> 02:59.520
Okay, okay, jeez. Ugh!

52
03:00.680 --> 03:01.600
Pa--

53
03:05.680 --> 03:06.440
Where is she?

54
03:06.440 --> 03:08.720
So, one bucket of ice and two bottles of liquor.

55
03:09.480 --> 03:10.800
Anything else?

56
03:10.800 --> 03:12.200
Get me a drink server.

57
03:12.200 --> 03:15.680
Whoa, Peem. What mood are you in today?

58
03:16.360 --> 03:17.360
Can we get a pretty one?

59
03:17.360 --> 03:21.040
Oh, hello. I'll be the one serving the drinks for you, sir.

60
03:21.640 --> 03:25.240
Well, today is our club's birthday, so...

61
03:25.240 --> 03:27.280
I heard there's an auction here, right?

62
03:27.800 --> 03:28.560
Yes.

63
03:29.160 --> 03:30.560
Then let's join it.

64
03:30.560 --> 03:32.920
The show is about to begin. Shall we go now?

65
03:34.320 --> 03:35.600
What? You're going now?

66
03:35.600 --> 03:37.000
Of course, what are you waiting for?

67
03:37.360 --> 03:39.920
These guys just can't wait when it comes to women.

68
03:43.800 --> 03:44.960
Hey.

69
03:44.960 --> 03:47.079
Why did you ask me to come to a place like this?

70
03:47.560 --> 03:50.400
So many women I'm getting goosebumps.

71
03:52.840 --> 03:54.720
Soon, you'll get more goosebumps.

72
03:54.720 --> 03:56.520
Huh? More?

73
03:57.360 --> 03:58.600
I don't think I can take it.

74
04:01.400 --> 04:02.360
Wait for me.

75
04:11.440 --> 04:13.160
Look at you smiling so happily.

76
04:13.560 --> 04:14.760
Where's Boy?

77
04:14.760 --> 04:16.800
He left with a girl a while ago.

78
04:17.279 --> 04:19.120
- As expected of him. - Right.

79
04:19.480 --> 04:20.560
They're all pretty.

80
04:36.920 --> 04:41.040
Hey, hey, hey, that's the sugar baby girl we met at the restaurant.

81
04:41.640 --> 04:43.240
Whoa, she's so pretty.

82
04:44.320 --> 04:45.280
Wow.

83
04:45.760 --> 04:46.960
Very pretty.

84
04:58.320 --> 05:00.760
Tell your Sis I want Parn to be my drink server.

85
05:00.760 --> 05:01.880
I'm buying 500 drinks.

86
05:01.880 --> 05:02.880
Huh?

87
05:02.880 --> 05:03.760
Okay.

88
05:04.520 --> 05:07.280
You're paying 200,000 for a drink server, Peem?

89
05:08.080 --> 05:09.160
That's crazy!

90
05:10.840 --> 05:12.880
This one? She won't come if I pay too little.

91
05:14.360 --> 05:15.440
It's 200,000, though?

92
05:30.760 --> 05:31.720
Thank you.

93
05:33.680 --> 05:34.720
Where's mine?

94
05:52.040 --> 05:53.480
- Mister! - Hey!

95
05:56.840 --> 05:58.000
I'm sorry.

96
06:06.960 --> 06:08.360
Then you wipe it for me.

97
07:18.880 --> 07:21.040
Your brand's pop-up event you want to hold at my mall,

98
07:22.440 --> 07:23.640
I'm cancelling it for now.

99
07:25.240 --> 07:27.200
- What? - Please excuse me.

100
07:28.880 --> 07:30.200
You said you're okay before?

101
07:30.560 --> 07:32.200
We're going to sign the contract next week.

102
07:45.600 --> 07:47.360
Hey, calm down.

103
07:51.360 --> 07:52.600
Peem.

104
07:52.600 --> 07:55.120
You two discussed it and it's going well. Why are you cancelling it now?

105
07:56.159 --> 07:58.200
There's another brand with a better offer.

106
08:01.920 --> 08:03.000
- Hey. - Hey.

107
08:04.160 --> 08:05.200
This girl.

108
08:06.200 --> 08:07.880
It's okay. I'll talk to her.

109
08:09.160 --> 08:10.040
Jeez.

110
08:17.480 --> 08:20.200
You said you don't want to see my face. Why are you here again?

111
08:21.520 --> 08:22.800
My friends wanted to hang out.

112
08:22.800 --> 08:24.080
Your friends wanted to hang out?

113
08:24.640 --> 08:27.080
Or did you actually bring them here to give me trouble?

114
08:31.760 --> 08:33.280
Do you really like this kind of job?

115
08:33.840 --> 08:36.679
A job that requires you to tolerate being look down on and being harassed?

116
08:37.720 --> 08:38.960
With me, you just wouldn't give in.

117
08:38.960 --> 08:40.799
Your pride was always in the way of everything.

118
08:41.640 --> 08:42.960
Why did you give in and do that just now?

119
08:46.440 --> 08:47.680
It's work.

120
08:49.680 --> 08:51.080
Then everything you did with me all this time

121
08:52.520 --> 08:53.800
was all work to you?

122
08:57.160 --> 08:59.080
Was it, Parn? Answer me!

123
09:02.560 --> 09:04.040
So if I pay today,

124
09:05.120 --> 09:06.520
I can do it now.

125
09:10.920 --> 09:11.640
Ms. Peem!

126
09:35.280 --> 09:37.120
Hey, Peem.

127
09:37.120 --> 09:39.960
You just disappeared. You even left your bag.

128
09:46.200 --> 09:47.480
What's wrong?

129
09:47.480 --> 09:48.720
They all left?

130
09:49.280 --> 09:53.400
Yeah. They're all bummed since you cancelled Neung's pop-up store.

131
09:54.360 --> 09:56.000
I'm leaving too.

132
09:56.000 --> 09:57.280
What about you? Are you leaving now?

133
09:58.240 --> 09:59.400
Mm.

134
09:59.720 --> 10:01.240
Don't worry.

135
10:01.240 --> 10:02.720
I'll find my way back myself.

136
10:04.280 --> 10:08.800
You're drunk. Don't drive home yourself, okay?

137
10:08.800 --> 10:09.800
Mm.

138
10:10.720 --> 10:11.920
I'll get a U Drink.

139
10:14.160 --> 10:16.480
Leave soon. And call me when you're home.

140
10:17.160 --> 10:18.880
It's an order from your gay friend.

141
10:20.480 --> 10:21.360
Fine.

142
10:22.640 --> 10:23.760
Are you sure you're okay?

143
10:24.840 --> 10:25.880
Yeah.

144
10:26.280 --> 10:27.320
I'm leaving then?

145
10:28.840 --> 10:29.720
Bye.

146
10:36.880 --> 10:39.120
Thank you for using our service.

147
10:57.960 --> 10:59.080
Who's that?

148
10:59.720 --> 11:00.880
Open the door.

149
11:05.200 --> 11:08.360
What? Are you banging someone? Why can't you open it?

150
11:10.160 --> 11:12.880
Why can't my money stop you?

151
11:24.040 --> 11:27.240
How come my money isn't as valuable as others'?

152
11:36.320 --> 11:37.640
All this time,

153
11:39.960 --> 11:42.200
have you ever loved me at all?

154
12:10.200 --> 12:12.160
Why did you get so drunk?

155
12:23.200 --> 12:24.280
Don't go.

156
12:29.320 --> 12:30.960
Can you stay here for now?

157
12:53.080 --> 12:55.440
I thought you weren't going to open the door for me.

158
12:58.880 --> 13:00.280
I tried to forget,

159
13:01.640 --> 13:03.080
but I couldn't.

160
13:39.920 --> 13:40.760
Are you hurt?

161
13:59.160 --> 14:00.600
♪ Don't let this go to waste ♪

162
14:00.600 --> 14:02.800
♪ Baby, we can work it out ♪

163
14:02.800 --> 14:04.920
♪ I just wanna let you know ♪

164
14:04.920 --> 14:06.680
♪ I wanna be with you ♪

165
14:06.680 --> 14:08.200
♪ I wanna be with you ♪

166
14:09.160 --> 14:10.560
♪ You ♪

167
14:11.240 --> 14:12.320
♪ You ♪

168
14:12.320 --> 14:15.120
♪ I wanna be with you ♪

169
14:17.440 --> 14:19.800
♪ I hope that we can work it out ♪

170
14:19.800 --> 14:21.880
♪ But I know that you have your doubts ♪

171
14:21.880 --> 14:23.520
♪ I wanna be with you ♪

172
14:24.120 --> 14:25.440
♪ Don't you wanna be with me? ♪

173
14:26.160 --> 14:28.480
♪ I think about you night and day ♪

174
14:28.480 --> 14:30.560
♪ And I just want you here with me ♪

175
14:30.560 --> 14:32.080
♪ I wanna be with you ♪

176
14:32.080 --> 14:34.040
♪ You know it is the truth ♪

177
14:34.040 --> 14:35.400
♪ Don't run away ♪

178
14:35.400 --> 14:37.600
♪ We can't let this go to waste ♪

179
14:37.600 --> 14:41.120
♪ I don't want nobody else, else ♪

180
14:41.800 --> 14:43.160
Ms. Peem.

181
14:48.040 --> 14:49.200
Can you be gentle?

182
15:04.160 --> 15:08.240
♪ But with you I think I found home ♪

183
15:08.760 --> 15:17.040
♪ Like every wave will Find its way back into the big blue ♪

184
15:17.040 --> 15:19.560
♪ I will find my way to you ♪

185
15:19.560 --> 15:22.320
♪ And like a harvest moon ♪

186
15:22.320 --> 15:24.720
♪ Turn from darkness into gold ♪

187
15:24.720 --> 15:26.840
♪ That’s when you’ll know ♪

188
15:27.400 --> 15:29.840
♪ That you’ll find home ♪

189
15:29.840 --> 15:37.120
♪ So here we go Now slowly open up your eyes ♪

190
15:37.800 --> 15:40.080
♪ Let me be your guide ♪

191
15:40.600 --> 15:44.000
♪ Stepping stones together ♪

192
15:44.000 --> 15:47.680
♪ Do you see it now ♪

193
15:48.400 --> 15:50.560
♪ You’re still that child ♪

194
15:51.040 --> 15:59.400
♪ Like every wave will Find its way back into the big blue ♪

195
15:59.400 --> 16:01.840
♪ I will find my way to you ♪

196
16:01.840 --> 16:04.480
♪ And like a harvest moon ♪

197
16:04.480 --> 16:06.880
♪ Turn from darkness into gold ♪

198
16:06.880 --> 16:09.000
♪ That’s how you know ♪

199
16:09.640 --> 16:11.920
♪ That you found home ♪

200
16:21.680 --> 16:22.920
I missed you so much.

201
18:05.040 --> 18:06.680
I'll transfer the money to you.

202
18:09.480 --> 18:10.480
So no one can talk behind my back,

203
18:11.360 --> 18:12.760
saying I dragged you into bed but didn't pay.

204
18:23.920 --> 18:25.080
I guess it's enough.

205
18:29.240 --> 18:30.320
I made a mistake.

206
18:31.360 --> 18:32.800
I was drunk last night.

207
18:33.200 --> 18:35.520
Consider this me paying for my own mistake.

208
18:41.840 --> 18:42.960
Please get out.

209
18:47.240 --> 18:48.160
Get out!

210
18:57.120 --> 18:58.400
Get out!

211
19:02.680 --> 19:06.280
♪ I want to slap myself in the mouth ♪

212
19:06.280 --> 19:09.600
♪ Why did I say that? ♪

213
19:09.600 --> 19:15.840
♪ Making something so simple so complicated ♪

214
19:18.160 --> 19:25.280
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

215
19:25.280 --> 19:30.160
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

216
19:30.560 --> 19:33.240
♪ I don't understand ♪

217
19:33.240 --> 19:38.600
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

218
19:38.600 --> 19:43.520
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪

219
19:43.920 --> 19:50.560
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

220
19:57.000 --> 19:58.400
She hasn't showed up to work yet?

221
19:58.400 --> 19:59.320
No, sir.

222
20:01.840 --> 20:03.720
Is she having a meeting somewhere?

223
20:03.720 --> 20:04.520
No, sir.

224
20:12.480 --> 20:13.680
Hey, Peem.

225
20:13.680 --> 20:15.560
Where have you been? Why didn't you answer my calls?

226
20:22.040 --> 20:24.520
Why is your heartbreak taking so long, huh?

227
20:25.120 --> 20:26.600
Come on. Who is it?

228
20:26.600 --> 20:29.640
Why is it that one minute you're good and the next you relapse, like you're bipolar?

229
20:32.640 --> 20:36.520
All this time I've known you, this is the most shaken I've ever seen you.

230
20:39.160 --> 20:40.160
I'm fine.

231
20:40.760 --> 20:41.680
Gosh.

232
20:41.680 --> 20:43.880
"I'm fine."

233
20:44.320 --> 20:46.280
You look like you're on the verge of death.

234
20:46.280 --> 20:48.360
Is there anything I should know, Peem?

235
20:55.680 --> 20:56.960
I went to Parn.

236
20:57.800 --> 20:58.760
Parn.

237
21:00.320 --> 21:01.680
Who's Parn?

238
21:03.560 --> 21:06.440
The one you were going to bring to meet me, but didn't come in the end?

239
21:07.920 --> 21:08.720
Yeah.

240
21:10.480 --> 21:12.520
What did you call her again? Parn?

241
21:18.800 --> 21:19.960
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

242
21:21.280 --> 21:23.240
Don't tell me it's the Parn from last night?

243
21:26.800 --> 21:30.760
That's why you got so mad when Neung told her to wipe the drink off his pants.

244
21:33.280 --> 21:35.680
I was wondering what the hell had gotten into you.

245
21:37.680 --> 21:40.400
So you were dating an escort?

246
21:57.680 --> 21:58.960
(Successful transfer)

247
22:03.400 --> 22:04.440
Parn.

248
22:06.720 --> 22:07.720
Oh.

249
22:08.240 --> 22:09.400
Mr. Techin.

250
22:09.920 --> 22:11.400
Sis Mol told me you're probably here.

251
22:13.680 --> 22:15.400
You didn't tell me you're opening a shop.

252
22:16.640 --> 22:18.080
It's not finished yet.

253
22:21.400 --> 22:24.240
But I think it's almost finished.

254
22:27.160 --> 22:28.200
Pan,

255
22:29.040 --> 22:30.280
Pastry-ne.

256
22:30.920 --> 22:32.720
Your name, Parn, and...

257
22:33.360 --> 22:34.320
Ne?

258
22:35.760 --> 22:36.880
Is it from Phakanee?

259
22:43.960 --> 22:45.000
Parn.

260
22:46.040 --> 22:47.800
If Ms. Peem wants to know about me,

261
22:49.800 --> 22:51.240
you can tell her.

262
22:53.320 --> 22:54.600
She won't listen.

263
23:00.520 --> 23:03.040
Almost ten million? I'm losing my mind.

264
23:03.920 --> 23:06.320
Just for today alone, how much did you pay?

265
23:06.320 --> 23:08.520
What's your getting-in-bed fee?

266
23:11.800 --> 23:12.720
One million.

267
23:12.720 --> 23:14.600
Huh?! One million?

268
23:16.560 --> 23:19.120
Can you try saying 3,000?

269
23:20.560 --> 23:21.840
Or maybe 4,000?

270
23:23.640 --> 23:25.040
Or maybe over ten thousand?

271
23:26.480 --> 23:27.800
Alright, hundred thousand?

272
23:29.480 --> 23:31.640
Are you crazy? One million?

273
23:32.080 --> 23:35.920
From what you've told me, there wasn't a single moment where she asked you for money.

274
23:35.920 --> 23:39.160
You're the one who kept showing off, paying loads of money. I'm genuinely shocked.

275
23:43.520 --> 23:45.400
Stop making excuses.

276
23:45.400 --> 23:48.080
You love her, so you pay for her. That's it.

277
23:49.120 --> 23:52.040
And why did you bring David along to show off to her?

278
23:52.680 --> 23:54.600
Because she was there with Techin.

279
23:54.600 --> 23:57.800
Peem, it's just me here. Stop being so stubborn.

280
24:02.920 --> 24:04.840
Fine, I was irritated.

281
24:06.360 --> 24:09.000
Irritated? You're jealous!

282
24:09.000 --> 24:10.720
It's called being jealous.

283
24:10.720 --> 24:11.560
I wasn't.

284
24:11.560 --> 24:12.960
Don't deny it.

285
24:12.960 --> 24:15.480
You were being all touchy with David,

286
24:15.480 --> 24:17.160
not because you felt irritated,

287
24:17.160 --> 24:19.080
but because you're jealous.

288
24:19.080 --> 24:20.760
Jealous. Jealous.

289
24:21.360 --> 24:23.120
There's no way it's because you're irritated.

290
24:25.280 --> 24:29.080
It's like, "You have a new guy? I can have a new guy too."

291
24:29.400 --> 24:30.320
Right?

292
24:33.080 --> 24:33.800
Yeah.

293
24:36.680 --> 24:37.640
You poor thing.

294
24:38.360 --> 24:40.200
If you love her and miss her so much

295
24:40.200 --> 24:42.560
that you'll act confused and go to her place when you're drunk

296
24:42.560 --> 24:44.400
even though she already has a new boyfriend,

297
24:45.160 --> 24:48.360
you need to start thinking about how you're going to deal with yourself.

298
24:57.040 --> 24:58.600
I need to stop loving her, right?

299
24:59.600 --> 25:00.440
Yeah.

300
25:18.880 --> 25:20.280
Hello, Dad.

301
25:21.360 --> 25:22.640
Oh, Peem.

302
25:25.080 --> 25:26.280
Can I talk to you for a sec?

303
25:34.880 --> 25:37.560
You're late for work. Some days, you didn't show up at all.

304
25:37.560 --> 25:39.160
You get drunk all the time.

305
25:39.640 --> 25:42.360
Apart from David's matter, you barely touch anything else.

306
25:43.200 --> 25:45.440
You even kept a client waiting in a meeting.

307
25:45.920 --> 25:48.080
The documents weren't signed. The checks won't go through.

308
25:49.560 --> 25:50.880
What is going on, Peem?

309
25:52.720 --> 25:53.920
I'm sorry, Dad.

310
25:54.960 --> 25:57.360
Work has been piling up on your end for a week now.

311
25:57.360 --> 26:00.200
Do you need to get in the mood before you can sign it?

312
26:01.120 --> 26:03.600
You can't work like this. The company needs to keep going.

313
26:03.600 --> 26:05.040
Now, everything has ground to a halt.

314
26:05.720 --> 26:07.400
How are the others supposed to get their work done?

315
26:09.920 --> 26:11.520
I'll be better.

316
26:13.120 --> 26:15.480
Just go back to being your old self, Peem.

317
26:17.200 --> 26:20.400
Seriously, what's going on?

318
26:24.360 --> 26:26.840
I will go back to being my old self, Dad.

319
26:29.160 --> 26:31.240
I want to know, as your father.

320
26:34.440 --> 26:35.680
What happened?

321
26:45.320 --> 26:48.520
Does this woman really affect you this much?

322
26:54.040 --> 26:56.200
Peem, it's okay to be sad.

323
26:57.360 --> 27:01.360
But you can't let your personal issues ruin everything like this.

324
27:18.960 --> 27:20.320
Whoa!

325
27:20.320 --> 27:21.520
Can I eat them now?

326
27:21.520 --> 27:23.200
They all look so tasty.

327
27:23.200 --> 27:24.240
Try them for me.

328
27:24.560 --> 27:26.160
And tell me if they're good or not.

329
27:26.160 --> 27:27.000
Sure.

330
27:29.840 --> 27:31.040
Whoa!

331
27:34.120 --> 27:35.280
Mmm.

332
27:35.800 --> 27:37.600
It's so soft and not too sweet.

333
27:37.600 --> 27:38.720
What do you think, Miew?

334
27:42.200 --> 27:43.080
Miew.

335
27:44.360 --> 27:45.360
Miew!

336
27:46.680 --> 27:48.200
Parn asked you. Didn't you hear?

337
27:48.200 --> 27:51.080
Oh, right, it's very soft. It melted in my mouth.

338
27:52.640 --> 27:53.640
Mmm.

339
27:57.560 --> 27:59.480
What about you? How are you?

340
28:05.440 --> 28:08.040
Okay, you don't have to say anything.

341
28:08.360 --> 28:09.680
I can tell it from your face.

342
28:32.800 --> 28:33.920
Your shop looks nice.

343
28:36.800 --> 28:37.800
Thank you.

344
28:39.160 --> 28:41.480
But you didn't come here to admire my shop, did you?

345
28:42.640 --> 28:46.440
You know that Peem will have to take over the company from me, right?

346
28:47.760 --> 28:48.680
Yes.

347
28:49.760 --> 28:53.200
Honestly, I don't have a problem if she likes women.

348
28:54.360 --> 28:55.880
But I have a problem

349
28:56.680 --> 28:58.120
with her loving someone like you.

350
29:00.360 --> 29:01.400
Like me?

351
29:01.960 --> 29:02.960
Yes.

352
29:03.520 --> 29:04.880
A sex worker like you.

353
29:07.560 --> 29:10.080
Even though you don't do that anymore,

354
29:10.080 --> 29:13.000
those who knew you, or have met you,

355
29:13.000 --> 29:15.720
will still remember what you've done.

356
29:18.960 --> 29:20.640
Even if Peem doesn't care,

357
29:21.840 --> 29:24.080
people in her social circle

358
29:25.960 --> 29:27.640
won't stop talking about it.

359
29:31.800 --> 29:35.800
The fact that Peem's mother is a sex worker is bad enough as it is.

360
29:37.200 --> 29:39.600
I don't want her to follow in my footsteps.

361
29:42.800 --> 29:44.080
If you love Peem,

362
29:45.480 --> 29:46.520
let her go.

363
29:56.400 --> 30:00.080
And if you need money, contact my secretary.

364
30:06.440 --> 30:07.280
Come on.

365
30:09.000 --> 30:11.040
Parn, what did he say to you?

366
30:21.960 --> 30:23.720
(Mom)

367
30:29.280 --> 30:31.520
Parn, your mom is calling.

368
30:32.200 --> 30:34.120
Hey, you should just ignore it for now.

369
30:38.520 --> 30:40.400
If I ignore it, she'll keep calling.

370
30:41.440 --> 30:42.520
In the end, I'll have to answer.

371
30:47.000 --> 30:48.040
Parn.

372
30:48.040 --> 30:49.600
Send me some money.

373
30:50.920 --> 30:52.360
I'm in real trouble.

374
30:54.160 --> 30:55.760
I don't have it, Mom.

375
30:55.760 --> 30:57.360
I don't have any more for you.

376
31:07.120 --> 31:08.040
What did she say?

377
31:08.520 --> 31:09.800
She said she didn't have anymore.

378
31:13.960 --> 31:15.040
How's that possible?

379
31:16.160 --> 31:19.000
I'm not stupid enough to believe she doesn't have any money.

380
31:22.120 --> 31:24.160
It’s no surprise that she doesn’t have any.

381
31:25.360 --> 31:26.880
She spent millions paying her father's debts.

382
31:27.720 --> 31:28.920
She doesn't have it.

383
31:29.520 --> 31:31.240
And do you have it to give to me, huh?

384
31:33.160 --> 31:35.760
A lowly salary man like you doesn't have the money to give to me.

385
31:36.880 --> 31:38.880
If you don't have it, I don't need your opinion.

386
31:43.840 --> 31:45.480
You have Parn's girlfriend's phone number, right?

387
31:47.080 --> 31:49.960
Parn doesn't have it, but she does.

388
31:50.840 --> 31:51.680
Call her.

389
31:52.360 --> 31:53.440
Leave her alone, Dad.

390
31:56.240 --> 31:57.480
I said call her.

391
32:00.400 --> 32:01.160
Mom.

392
32:04.240 --> 32:05.280
I said call her!

393
32:14.080 --> 32:15.520
Miew, are you putting in any effort?

394
32:15.880 --> 32:16.960
It hit my foot.

395
32:16.960 --> 32:18.520
See? You're not lifting it.

396
32:18.520 --> 32:20.760
I am lifting it. Why are you so whiny?

397
32:20.760 --> 32:22.680
You ate a lot too.

398
32:22.680 --> 32:24.400
Just get the chair.

399
32:30.320 --> 32:32.600
You did the right thing, not giving your mom the money.

400
32:32.600 --> 32:35.120
Stop it. Don't bring it up.

401
32:37.400 --> 32:39.720
Alright, let's go home. I'll give you a ride.

402
32:40.360 --> 32:43.480
Hey, how about we stop and pick up some food?

403
32:43.480 --> 32:44.680
Let's eat at your place.

404
32:55.160 --> 32:56.320
What is it, Pong?

405
33:02.640 --> 33:04.840
Here. The money you want.

406
33:14.440 --> 33:15.720
Thank you so much.

407
33:15.720 --> 33:18.160
I'll have Parn find the money to pay you back as soon as possible.

408
33:19.440 --> 33:20.560
Dad.

409
33:21.320 --> 33:22.320
What's going on?

410
33:25.480 --> 33:27.480
Where are you taking my money?

411
33:27.480 --> 33:28.800
It's not your money.

412
33:30.560 --> 33:32.240
Why are you giving my dad money?

413
33:32.240 --> 33:34.600
Your family is in trouble. I'm just trying to help.

414
33:34.600 --> 33:37.160
I didn't ask you to. And it's none of your business.

415
33:38.120 --> 33:39.440
Stop it. Give me back my money.

416
33:39.440 --> 33:40.320
No!

417
33:41.040 --> 33:44.520
If you don't give this to me, where do you expect me to find the money?

418
33:44.520 --> 33:47.120
Wherever you can, but not from Ms. Peem.

419
33:48.000 --> 33:48.800
Parn!

420
33:48.800 --> 33:50.080
- Don't! - Dad!

421
33:51.440 --> 33:53.960
I'll take all the money back if you touch Parn again.

422
34:14.280 --> 34:16.360
From now on, stay away from my family.

423
34:19.679 --> 34:21.920
You're in this much trouble and you still dare to refuse?

424
34:23.560 --> 34:25.000
I know that you have money.

425
34:25.480 --> 34:26.920
But I don't want your money.

426
34:27.679 --> 34:30.440
The money you used to pay off my dad's debt, I'll pay you back.

427
34:30.960 --> 34:31.880
No need.

428
34:31.880 --> 34:34.600
I will. I don't want to be indebted to anyone.

429
34:36.840 --> 34:37.719
Especially you.

430
34:42.400 --> 34:43.719
Do you hate me that much?

431
34:45.760 --> 34:48.880
If you love Peem, let her go.

432
34:51.480 --> 34:52.520
That's right.

433
34:54.199 --> 34:55.440
I hate you so much.

434
34:59.400 --> 35:01.320
You hate me so much you don't want anything to do with me?

435
35:10.000 --> 35:11.160
Then I'll wait and see

436
35:12.040 --> 35:13.600
how you're going to find the money to pay me back.

437
35:15.400 --> 35:17.240
It's five million, Parn, not five hundred.

438
35:20.840 --> 35:23.000
But you have an easy way to make money, don't you?

439
35:25.120 --> 35:25.960
You're right.

440
35:26.480 --> 35:29.880
Don't forget that I'm Paradise's top angel.

441
35:42.200 --> 35:44.480
Parn! Why the hell did you have to butt in?

442
35:44.480 --> 35:45.680
Why did you stop her?

443
35:45.680 --> 35:46.880
Where am I supposed to get the money from now?

444
35:46.880 --> 35:48.720
Hit me. Hit me now.

445
35:48.720 --> 35:49.960
I don't have any more for you.

446
35:50.360 --> 35:53.280
Even if you beat me to death, I don't have any money to give you.

447
35:56.720 --> 35:58.600
You want those loan sharks to kill me, right?

448
35:59.920 --> 36:00.880
Huh?!

449
36:01.600 --> 36:03.640
You've been saying that to me all my life.

450
36:04.080 --> 36:08.040
I paid off your debts countless times but you kept going back to borrow from them.

451
36:08.440 --> 36:09.480
You never stopped.

452
36:09.960 --> 36:11.720
This time, I really don't have any to give you.

453
36:12.720 --> 36:15.920
You said you don't have money but you're opening a new shop.

454
36:16.240 --> 36:17.920
Just sell your shop and give me the money.

455
36:17.920 --> 36:18.920
No!

456
36:18.920 --> 36:20.000
Parn.

457
36:20.000 --> 36:21.200
No, Mom.

458
36:21.200 --> 36:22.280
I'm not selling it.

459
36:25.120 --> 36:27.080
I'll use this shop to make a living.

460
36:27.440 --> 36:30.240
All this time, I've done what I could to help.

461
36:31.280 --> 36:34.760
But if that makes you think I have to be responsible for everything you do,

462
36:35.960 --> 36:37.480
I will stop now.

463
36:40.280 --> 36:43.160
From now on, I won't give you two any more money.

464
36:44.800 --> 36:46.480
I want to try living for myself.

465
36:59.600 --> 37:01.400
Parn! You ungrateful child!

466
37:02.040 --> 37:03.760
Your life will never prosper!

467
37:10.040 --> 37:11.200
Who do you think you are?

468
37:11.920 --> 37:15.200
Don't forget that I'm Paradise's top angel.

469
37:16.160 --> 37:17.000
Of course.

470
37:17.440 --> 37:20.720
Paradise Club's Angel can make money easily just by selling her body.

471
37:20.720 --> 37:23.720
Go ahead. Sell your body until you die.

472
37:24.200 --> 37:25.880
Since you've made your choice, go all out.

473
37:36.280 --> 37:38.120
Should I go see it with my own eyes?

474
37:40.640 --> 37:42.040
So I can finally get over it?

475
37:47.240 --> 37:48.960
Oh, Ms. Peem.

476
37:53.680 --> 37:55.120
Will Parn be in the auction today?

477
37:55.920 --> 37:57.320
Do you want to see Parn?

478
37:58.600 --> 37:59.520
No.

479
38:02.600 --> 38:04.720
Parn is no longer working here.

480
38:05.600 --> 38:08.360
The last day she came here was the day you came.

481
38:08.920 --> 38:11.720
Sis Mol called Parn and asked her to come and help.

482
38:12.640 --> 38:14.040
She called her herself?

483
38:19.480 --> 38:21.520
Let's talk somewhere else.

484
38:26.680 --> 38:30.440
Since Parn started seeing you, she hasn't been working here anymore.

485
38:30.440 --> 38:32.440
She even asked me

486
38:32.440 --> 38:34.440
to help tell Sis Mol she's going to quit.

487
38:35.480 --> 38:36.800
But she's still accepting clients.

488
38:37.360 --> 38:39.280
She even went out with Techin.

489
38:39.280 --> 38:40.800
Oh my. Well.

490
38:41.440 --> 38:45.160
Mr. Techin has been Parn's client for so long.

491
38:45.160 --> 38:47.720
So long I think they've become friends.

492
38:47.720 --> 38:51.680
I can't say much because I don't want to reveal clients' secrets,

493
38:52.200 --> 38:57.320
but I can assure you there is nothing between Parn and Mr. Techin.

494
39:00.000 --> 39:03.720
But I don't get it. Why did she come back to work here?

495
39:07.680 --> 39:09.680
Sis Mol owed ten million to a loan shark.

496
39:10.520 --> 39:14.320
Parn came to help make money to pay off the debt,

497
39:14.320 --> 39:15.840
so they wouldn't take over this place.

498
39:15.840 --> 39:19.880
But after the debt had been settled, Parn told Sis Mol she's going to stop right away.

499
39:20.800 --> 39:23.880
The day you came here was Paradise's Birthday.

500
39:23.880 --> 39:25.960
Sis Mol asked Parn to come join the event.

501
39:26.280 --> 39:27.560
Parn.

502
39:28.880 --> 39:29.960
Ms. Peem is here.

503
39:31.040 --> 39:33.560
Parn, she's buying 500 drinks. What do you say?

504
39:33.560 --> 39:37.600
Hey, but you're not here to work. You're just here for the event.

505
39:38.120 --> 39:39.920
Right, Sis only asked you to join.

506
39:40.280 --> 39:41.280
That's right.

507
39:43.680 --> 39:46.600
If I go in, she might listen to my explanation.

508
39:47.120 --> 39:49.440
Parn wasn't going to be in the auction.

509
39:50.160 --> 39:54.120
But since it's you, she wanted to be your drink server.

510
39:56.640 --> 40:00.520
She's running a bakery now. She's not coming back to work here.

511
40:02.200 --> 40:04.080
Do you know where her shop is?

512
40:05.720 --> 40:09.000
She asked me not to tell you no matter what.

513
40:36.680 --> 40:38.920
You got dumped too?

514
40:39.920 --> 40:41.160
Is that why you're drinking here?

515
40:43.840 --> 40:45.000
Who dumped me?

516
40:46.400 --> 40:47.400
Parn, of course.

517
40:48.160 --> 40:49.800
She's not accepting any more jobs.

518
40:53.400 --> 40:55.320
I'm bummed she stopped accepting jobs.

519
40:55.840 --> 40:57.200
But I'm not sad.

520
41:02.360 --> 41:03.600
Didn't she tell you

521
41:05.080 --> 41:06.280
that I'm gay?

522
41:16.240 --> 41:17.640
I'll tell you then.

523
41:18.480 --> 41:21.800
David, that investor from Singapore,

524
41:22.360 --> 41:24.160
the one you're flaunting in my face,

525
41:25.880 --> 41:27.240
he's my boyfriend.

526
41:29.000 --> 41:33.520
I hired Parn to pretend to be my girlfriend to make my parents happy.

527
41:34.800 --> 41:37.080
And I asked Parn to keep it a secret.

528
41:43.200 --> 41:45.160
You're saying I misunderstood?

529
42:03.920 --> 42:05.240
You misunderstood Parn.

530
42:06.840 --> 42:09.560
Don't wait until it's too late to get her back

531
42:09.560 --> 42:10.960
before you get yourself together.

532
42:11.760 --> 42:14.240
Even though we're business rivals,

533
42:14.960 --> 42:18.080
I'm rooting for you on this one.

534
42:20.720 --> 42:22.120
Because Parn really loves you.

535
43:20.800 --> 43:22.640
Pan Pastry-ne.

536
43:24.880 --> 43:26.000
Why "Ne"?

537
43:27.640 --> 43:29.160
What an unimpressive name.

538
43:32.920 --> 43:34.200
You're going out of business for sure.

539
43:45.960 --> 43:49.320
How well could someone like you possibly run a shop?

540
44:03.640 --> 44:04.840
I knew it. It's just a small shop.

541
44:08.520 --> 44:09.640
Opening day.

542
44:16.160 --> 44:18.840
- First order! - First order!

543
44:18.840 --> 44:22.680
Ms. Peem, what should we do with these?

544
44:22.680 --> 44:25.160
Bring me a box to try. But I don't think it'll be good.

545
44:28.520 --> 44:29.520
Why didn't you accept the flowers?

546
44:29.520 --> 44:31.920
You have the right to send it. I have the right not to accept.

547
44:33.320 --> 44:34.120
What's wrong with you?

548
44:34.120 --> 44:35.840
What is wrong with you?

549
44:35.840 --> 44:38.560
You say you don't want to see me, but you keep coming.

550
44:40.480 --> 44:41.520
You don't love me anymore?

551
44:44.400 --> 44:51.320
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

552
44:51.320 --> 44:56.320
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

553
44:56.840 --> 44:59.520
♪ I don't understand ♪

554
44:59.520 --> 45:04.920
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

555
45:04.920 --> 45:08.080
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪
